tt-hw-debug: complete SPDX header coverage for upstream/

0003 converted the sources carrying the "// *" line-comment confidentiality
legend, but the trace/ block-comment sources and a number of files that never
had any header were left uncovered, so the tree could not be brought under the
SPDX license check. Finish the job so every upstream/ file carries a valid
identifier without changing RTL behavior:

  - Replace the remaining "/* ... */" confidentiality banners (trace/) with the
    repository's canonical Apache-2.0 SPDX header.
  - Add the Apache-2.0 SPDX header to the header-less Tenstorrent-authored
    generics, generated MMR RTL, package lists, and MMR spec YAMLs.
  - trace_axi_master.sv is third-party (ETH Zurich / University of Bologna): tag
    it with its own SPDX-License-Identifier: SHL-0.51 and leave the upstream
    copyright and Solderpad license text intact. No TT copyright is asserted.

